{
  "_source": "Cargus publishes no test subscription key (docs ch.1: the Ocp-Apim key is issued only after a portal subscription is approved by an administrator), so no live run was possible. Bodies: (a) counties + pudoPoints: VERBATIM real API responses that the OFFICIAL Cargus WooCommerce plugin 1.6.0 caches and ships in admin/locations/counties.json and admin/locations/pudo_locations.json (https://downloads.wordpress.org/plugin/cargus.1.6.0.zip, sha1 5a28a75877db9603caa6c4de1c23a63592aee8e8; written by admin/class-cargus-cron.php from GET Counties / GET PudoPoints); 3 of 1966 PUDO rows kept (one with StreetName, two with an empty StreetName, as 638 rows have). (b) everything else: \"Technical Documentation API Cargus\" V3 2.3.2 (https://www.cargus.ro/wp-content/uploads/DocumentationAPIV3-2.3.2-EN.pdf): LoginUser returns the token (3.1; plugins json_decode it to a string), Localities fields (4.3), pick-up point = the documented Sender object of the 9.7/9.8 examples (commas the PDF misses restored), Awbs POST returns the generated barcode (9.2; PrestaShop module stores it as a scalar; 9.7/9.8 show alphanumeric BarCode \"URGC10875236\"), DELETE Awbs returns true/false (9.5), AwbDocuments returns base64 (9.9), AwbTrace/WithRedirect fields Code/Type/MeasuredWeight/VolumetricWeight/ConfirmationName/Observation/ResponseCode/Event[Date,Description,LocalityName] (9.10) + EventId (9.12); dates in the docs format \"2019-10-24T12:33:12.035Z\". In (b) field names are the documented ones; ids, descriptions and dates of localities/trace events are illustrative (the PDF has no response samples for them).",
